            <ArticleTitle>Fatal rupture of a mycotic aneurysm of the right coronary artery post pneumococcal sepsis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>84-87</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Aneurysms of the coronary arteries are rare and mycotic coronary aneurysms are even rarer. We report a unique, yet unfortunately autopsy-proven fatal case of a ruptured atherosclerotic mycotic aneurysm of the right coronary artery with streptococcus pneumoniae in a non-immunocompromised patient resulting in cor tamponade and death.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
